1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:02,129
Do you know how we currently run

2
00:00:02,149 --> 00:00:03,517
our SALARY CYCLE?

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:06,429
Let's start with how it works today.

4
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:09,130
Today, our cycle runs

5
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:11,532
from JANUARY to DECEMBER

6
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:14,871
12 months, one cycle.

7
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:16,235
MERIT

8
00:00:16,255 --> 00:00:18,710
Expected market movement

9
00:00:18,790 --> 00:00:21,195
based on projected market

10
00:00:21,215 --> 00:00:22,510
and inflation trends

11
00:00:22,590 --> 00:00:24,275
Salary market data becomes

12
00:00:24,295 --> 00:00:26,384
available around NOVEMBER

13
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:27,651
BONUS

14
00:00:27,671 --> 00:00:30,887
Estimated Company Performance KPIs

15
00:00:32,210 --> 00:00:33,784
based on the information

16
00:00:33,804 --> 00:00:35,650
available by DECEMBER

17
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:39,164
Now, we're moving to a new cycle.

18
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:41,614
From APRIL to MARCH

19
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,639
It changes WHEN the

20
00:00:44,659 --> 00:00:46,560
information arrives

21
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:47,342
By JANUARY

22
00:00:47,362 --> 00:00:49,691
actual Company Performance

23
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:52,714
And by FEBRUARY

24
00:00:52,734 --> 00:00:55,287
actual market movement

25
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:59,860
Closer to market best practice

26
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:02,184
Decisions rest on more relevant,

27
00:01:02,204 --> 00:01:03,927
actual information

28
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:06,843
Merit increases and promotions

29
00:01:06,863 --> 00:01:08,767
take effect on APRIL 1

30
00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:12,374
That's where the cycle now begins.

31
00:01:12,650 --> 00:01:13,249
BONUS

32
00:01:13,269 --> 00:01:15,654
paid in the MARCH payroll

33
00:01:16,730 --> 00:01:18,815
MARCH is the last month

34
00:01:18,835 --> 00:01:20,290
of the cycle

35
00:01:20,370 --> 00:01:23,188
One thing that isn't changing

36
00:01:23,270 --> 00:01:24,690
Your PERFORMANCE APPRAISAL

37
00:01:24,709 --> 00:01:26,590
stays on the same schedule

38
00:01:26,670 --> 00:01:30,891
and it will still close

39
00:01:30,370 --> 00:01:31,074
One more thing -

40
00:01:31,094 --> 00:01:32,631
and it happens only once

41
00:01:33,470 --> 00:01:34,272
IMPLEMENTATION YEAR ONLY:

42
00:01:34,292 --> 00:01:35,592
15 months instead of 12

43
00:01:40,270 --> 00:01:42,598
ILLUSTRATIVE EXAMPLE

44
00:01:42,618 --> 00:01:44,590
a 5% merit increase

45
00:01:44,670 --> 00:01:49,240
5% ÷ 12 = 0.4167%

46
00:01:49,260 --> 00:01:49,450
per month

47
00:01:49,470 --> 00:01:51,990
Multiply that by 15 months

48
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:54,928
and the equivalent becomes

49
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:55,650
6.25%

50
00:01:55,670 --> 00:01:59,051
The merit percentage hasn't changed -

51
00:01:59,071 --> 00:02:00,390
only the months it covers

52
00:02:00,470 --> 00:02:02,220
APRIL to MARCH

53
00:02:02,970 --> 00:02:06,040
That's the one to remember.

54
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:07,890
Have questions?

55
00:02:07,970 --> 00:02:09,538
Please contact your HR personnel

56
00:02:09,558 --> 00:02:10,858
for support.
